<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vengi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vengi is a historical region of coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the deltas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Godavari rivers, named after its old capital near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eluru">Eluru</a>. Conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a> around 624, it became the kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-chalukyas">Eastern Chalukyas</a>, who ruled it until the eleventh century, when it was united with the Chola empire.</p></div>
